---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const breadcrumbLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
  'itemListElement': [
    { '@type': 'ListItem', 'position': 1, 'name': 'Home', 'item': 'https://portfolioatlas.org' },
    { '@type': 'ListItem', 'position': 2, 'name': 'Terms of Use', 'item': 'https://portfolioatlas.org/terms' },
  ],
};
---

<Layout
  title="Terms of Use"
  description="Terms of use for PortfolioAtlas: how you can use our city cost data and FIRE calculations, what we license, and what we don't warrant."
  jsonLd={breadcrumbLd}
>
  <div class="container-narrow py-16 md:py-24">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <h1 class="font-serif text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold text-brand-950 mb-6">
        Terms of Use
      </h1>

      <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none text-gray-700 space-y-6">
        <p class="text-xl text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
          PortfolioAtlas is a free research tool. These terms cover what the site provides, how
          you may use our data, and what we do and do not promise.
        </p>

        <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl font-bold text-brand-950 mt-12 mb-4">Informational purposes only</h2>
        <p>
          Everything on this site - cost estimates, FIRE Numbers, backtest results, visa notes,
          and city ratings - is research and estimation for informational purposes only. It is
          not financial, tax, legal, or immigration advice. Costs vary with personal choices,
          exchange rates, and inflation, and visa rules change without notice. Consult qualified
          professionals before making relocation or retirement decisions.
        </p>

        <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl font-bold text-brand-950 mt-12 mb-4">Using our data</h2>
        <p>
          The PortfolioAtlas dataset (city cost estimates, FIRE Numbers, and scores) is our own
          research work. You are welcome to reference it: quote figures, cite city pages, and
          share links, with attribution to PortfolioAtlas and a link back to the page you used.
          What these terms do not permit is republishing the dataset in bulk, scraping it into a
          competing product, or reselling it. If you want to use the data beyond quotation and
          citation, <a href="mailto:chris@portfolioatlas.org">ask us</a>.
        </p>
        <p>
          The historical market returns behind our backtests come from Robert Shiller's public
          dataset (1871-2022), used under the Open Data Commons Public Domain Dedication and
          License (ODC-PDDL). Our thanks to that project; its data remains public domain.
        </p>

        <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl font-bold text-brand-950 mt-12 mb-4">No warranties</h2>
        <p>
          The site is provided as-is. We work hard to keep figures current (each city page shows
          its data vintage), but we do not warrant that any figure is accurate, complete, or up
          to date, and we are not liable for decisions made from it. Past market performance
          does not guarantee future results.
        </p>

        <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl font-bold text-brand-950 mt-12 mb-4">Third-party services</h2>
        <p>
          The newsletter runs on Substack under Substack's own terms. Links to external sites
          are provided for convenience; we do not control and are not responsible for their
          content. How we handle your data is covered separately in our
          <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a>.
        </p>

        <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl font-bold text-brand-950 mt-12 mb-4">Changes</h2>
        <p>
          If these terms change, we will update this page. Material changes will be noted on the
          blog.
        </p>
        <p class="text-sm text-gray-500">
          Published July 8, 2026. Questions? Contact
          <a href="mailto:chris@portfolioatlas.org">chris@portfolioatlas.org</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
